213 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 81 0 R
/E (The Smart Task Manager uses two primary MongoDB collections: Users and Tasks. MongoDB stores data in flexible JSON-like documents, which integrates well with Node.js and is suitable for applications where the data structure may evolve over time. The Users collection stores account information with encrypted passwords, while the Tasks collection stores all task-related data linked to the owning user via a foreign key reference \(userId\). This one-to-many relationship means one user can have multiple tasks, and each task belongs to exactly one user.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
